Raider Del Castillo Abalos
.PP
Theo Golik
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sh (1),
.BR bash (1),
.BR dash (1),
.BR execve (2),
.BR fork (2),
.BR waitpid (2),
.BR access (2),
.BR getenv (3)
.SH NOTES
.B hsh
is designed to match the behavior of
.BR sh (1)
for basic command execution. Error messages follow the same format, with the
program name matching argv[0] as required by POSIX.
.PP
The shell is intended for educational purposes to demonstrate:
.PP
.RS
- Process creation and management with fork/execve/waitpid
.RE
.RS
- Environment variable manipulation
.RE
.RS
- PATH-based executable resolution
.RE
.RS
- Interactive vs non-interactive I/O handling
.RE
.PP
For production use, consider more complete shells such as
.BR bash (1)
or
.BR dash (1).
